/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 64 0 R
/T (Cryptarithms are mathematical puzzles in which letters represent digits. A valid solution assigns one digit to each distinct letter, does not reuse a digit for another letter, and makes the arithmetic equation correct. A CSP represents a problem through variables, domains, and constraints. Backtracking builds an assignment step by step and reverses a choice when it violates a constraint. Column-wise checking \(pruning\) can reject invalid partial assignments before every letter is assigned, making the search more efficient.)
/E (Cryptarithms are mathematical puzzles in which letters represent digits. A valid solution assigns one digit to each distinct letter, does not reuse a digit for another letter, and makes the arithmetic equation correct. A CSP represents a problem through variables, domains, and constraints. Backtracking builds an assignment step by step and reverses a choice when it violates a constraint. Column-wise checking \(pruning\) can reject invalid partial assignments before every letter is assigned, making the search more efficient.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
