/T (The Cryptarithmetic Puzzle Solver demonstrates how a mathematical word puzzle can be modelled as a Constraint Satisfaction Problem. Each letter is assigned a unique digit, leading digits are kept non-zero, and the arithmetic equation is checked. Backtracking explores possible assignments while column pruning rejects invalid partial solutions early. The supplied output verifies SEND = 9567, MORE = 1085, and MONEY = 10652, so 9567 + 1085 = 10652.)
/E (The Cryptarithmetic Puzzle Solver demonstrates how a mathematical word puzzle can be modelled as a Constraint Satisfaction Problem. Each letter is assigned a unique digit, leading digits are kept non-zero, and the arithmetic equation is checked. Backtracking explores possible assignments while column pruning rejects invalid partial solutions early. The supplied output verifies SEND = 9567, MORE = 1085, and MONEY = 10652, so 9567 + 1085 = 10652.)
